  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 141 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nThe remainder of next week will continue to feature very hot \ntemperatures and the potential for daily Heat Advisories. The upper \nridge will center more over New Mexico, which will bring back north \nnorthwesterly flow through the week. Afternoon convection along the \nhigher terrain in Colorado could be driven southeast by any embedded \nshortwaves in the northwest flow aloft into northern Oklahoma during \nthe late evening and overnight hours, but currently the chances \nremain low. A weak cold front late in the week may bring some relief \nto the triple digit heat by next weekend.",
